<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<worksheet>
    <title>Problem 30 - Written Homework - MTH 204</title>

    <exercise>
        <statement>
            <p>
                This final homework exercise invites you to reflect on your
                learning in the course.
                To earn an <q>E</q>, you need to follow the directions and show
                honest effort and introspection, and of course write in your own
                words.
                Here's the prompt:
            </p>

            <p>
                <em>What's something about linear algebra you learned in MTH 204 that you found compelling, interesting, creative, or surprising? Are you curious about learning more? If so, what topics are you curious about? If not, why not?</em>
            </p>

            <p>
                You should type a 250-500 word essay in response (that's roughly
                1/2 to 3/4 of a page of single-spaced text).
                Proof-read your work; collegiate-quality writing is expected.
                When you are finished, print your essay and staple it 
                to this page.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>
</worksheet>